{"id": 28, "ts": 1780470977.176004, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I agree with my earlier provisional shift to **Candidate\u202fC**. The new information about Candidate\u202fD confirms my concerns: we have no evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication, and the notes describe him as \u201cmoody\u201d and \u201cregarded as a loner,\u201d which directly threatens the crew\u2011cooperation and communication criteria essential for long\u2011haul flights. Even though D shows strong problem\u2011solving, concentration, and responsibility, those strengths are outweighed by the lack of teamwork evidence and the perception of poor interpersonal style.\nThus D cannot be considered a viable alternative to B or C. Between B and C, I still lack concrete data on C\u2019s stress\u2011resilience and technical competence, but C\u2019s documented 100\u202f% reliability and ability to create a positive crew atmosphere address two non\u2011negotiable safety criteria. Until we obtain evidence that C cannot handle high\u2011pressure situations, my provisional recommendation remains **Candidate\u202fC**."}
